Subject: Stop the battery wave animation from redrawing the bar forever

The battery widget runs an infinite 60 fps wave animation. On a laptop this
keeps Quickshell's render thread busy all the time (measured ~55% CPU while
charging, ~99% together with cava/sysmon). The side-bar copy is created even
when the bar sits on top and animates unconditionally, so both are disabled.
The battery level itself still updates normally.

--- a/src/quickshell/bar/modules/system/BatWidget.qml	2026-11-13 14:59:16.234623201 +0700
+++ b/src/quickshell/bar/modules/system/BatWidget.qml	2026-11-13 14:59:16.236998471 +0700
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
         to: Math.PI * 2
         duration: batWidgetRoot.isCharging ? 1800 : 3600
         loops: Animation.Infinite
-        running: batWidgetRoot.showLayout && batWidgetRoot.moduleActive
+        running: false
     }
 
     Timer {
--- a/src/quickshell/bar/sidemodules/system/SideBatWidget.qml	2026-11-13 14:59:16.244513957 +0700
+++ b/src/quickshell/bar/sidemodules/system/SideBatWidget.qml	2026-11-13 14:59:16.246431327 +0700
@@ -65,7 +65,7 @@
         to: Math.PI * 2
         duration: sideBatRoot.isCharging ? 1800 : 3600
         loops: Animation.Infinite
-        running: sideBatRoot.showLayout && sideBatRoot.moduleActive
+        running: false
     }
 
     Timer {
